# .gitleaksignore — Findings to ignore during secret scanning
#
# Gitleaks v8 expects finding fingerprints (SHA-256 of each finding),
# rule IDs, or path: prefixes in this file. Bare file paths without a
# `path:` prefix are treated as fingerprints and will not match anything.
#
# No entries are currently required: scanner verification uses temporary
# fixtures created in an isolated temporary Git repository during the
# scanner-verification-test.sh script, so no credential-looking material
# is committed to AuroraOS history and nothing needs to be allowlisted here.
#
# If a legitimate finding must ever be excluded, add its fingerprint
# (obtained from a Gitleaks scan output) on its own line, with a comment
# documenting why. Never allowlist entire source directories or real
# credentials.
